    11	     Job-ID marked orphans outside running groups remain targets.
    12	  4. On memory pressure, kill eligible members of the largest job, allowing its wrapper
    13	     3 seconds to record failure. Re-inventory for up to 5 seconds, including new forks.
    14	Reads only /proc/<pid>/{status,stat,environ,cmdline} of our own uid; writes oom_score_adj.
    15	Python stdlib only. No process-group signals: every recipient must pass the allowlist.
    16	Usage: bin/memguard [--once] [--dry-run] [--interval S] [--min-available G] [--max-total G]
    17	                    [--log PATH] [--no-mail]
